<title>USA: Lexington Corporate to buy 3 properties.</title>
<headline>Lexington Corporate to buy 3 properties.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lexington Corporate Properties Inc said on Monday it has agreed to acquire three industrial properties for $14.17 million.</p>
<p>The properties will be net-leased to Johnson Controls Inc for 10 years, Lexington said.</p>
<p>The properties have an aggregate of 304,120 net rentable square feet located in Plymouth, Mich.; Oberlin, Ohio; and Tuscaloosa, Ala., Lexington said.</p>
<p>The initial annual rent will be $1.4 million and base rent increases will be based upon the consumer price index, not to exceed 4.5 per year, the company said.</p>
</text>
